# Practical 2 – SDN Infrastructure & S2D

**Q. What is SDN?**
A. Software Defined Networking separates the control plane from the data plane.

**Q. Advantage of SDN?**
A. Centralized and programmable network management.

**Q. What is Network Controller?**
A. The central component that manages SDN.

**Q. What is S2D?**
A. Storage Spaces Direct combines local disks into shared storage.

**Q. Benefit of S2D?**
A. High availability and scalable storage.

**Q. What is Failover Clustering?**
A. It provides continuous service during server failures.

