# Practical 3 – Service Manager

**Q. What is Service Manager?**
A. It is an IT service management tool.

**Q. Purpose of Service Manager?**
A. To manage incidents, problems, and change requests.

**Q. Why SQL Server is used?**
A. To store Service Manager data.

**Q. What is SSRS?**
A. SQL Server Reporting Services generates reports.

**Q. What is a Data Warehouse?**
A. A database used for reporting and analysis.

---

# Practical 4 & 5 – Orchestrator

**Q. What is Orchestrator?**
A. It automates IT tasks using runbooks.

**Q. What is a runbook?**
A. A workflow that automates tasks.

**Q. What is a monitor runbook?**
A. It waits for an event and starts automatically.

**Q. What is an activity?**
A. A single step inside a runbook.

**Q. What is an Integration Pack?**
A. A collection of activities for integrating products.

**Q. Why backup Orchestrator?**
A. To recover data after failures.

**Q. What is runbook throttling?**
A. It limits the number of simultaneous runbooks.

**Q. What is benchmarking?**
A. Measuring system performance.

**Q. Why recover the database?**
A. To restore lost Orchestrator data.

**Q. What is PowerPivot?**
A. An Excel tool for data analysis.

